  "narrative": "For the outcome_008 feature_055 claims with direction +1, positive signed estimates mean the exposed level is associated with a less negative CRISPR dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency, relative to the comparator. The outcome_008 approximate 10%-of-absolute-mean benchmark is 0.0282. The feature_055 audit gives a mixed picture. H100 shows a positive signed estimate of +0.0321 with interval +0.0014 to +0.0628, supporting that level_003 differs from level_002 and is similar to the original H98 level_003-versus-level_001 signal. However, H99, level_002 versus level_001, is null (-0.0006), and H104, level_004 versus level_001, is slightly opposite (-0.0045) with an upper confidence limit of +0.0257 below benchmark. Thus the effect is not part of a broad nonbaseline-level pattern; it looks more like a level_003-specific contrast. H99 is closed unresolved because the point is null and the interval only barely reaches threshold; H104 is rejected because clinically meaningful positive values are excluded by the upper bound. The stratum audits show that H105 and H106 are positive but imprecise, so the association is not obviously confined to feature_034=1. In contrast, H107 is a much stronger candidate: within feature_002=1, the signed estimate is +0.0614, interval +0.0181 to +0.1047. The point is well above benchmark and the interval excludes the null, but the lower bound is below benchmark, so I do not accept it on discovery evidence. H108, the feature_002=0 complement, is essentially null (+0.0035). This suggests possible subgroup heterogeneity or concentration of the signal in feature_002=1, and it raises a multiple-comparisons concern because H107 was one of several stratum audits. H107 is nevertheless the strongest remaining threshold-level signal, so I request independent validation for H107 to determine whether this is a replicable subgroup-specific association or a multiplicity artifact. For the remaining new screens, H84 and H85 are rejected because their upper confidence bounds are below the outcome_015 benchmark and their points are not threshold-aligned. H101 is extremely imprecise around zero and is closed unresolved. H102 has a positive point estimate above the low outcome_006 benchmark but includes the null and is inconsistent with cross-outcome feature_064 evidence, so it is deferred unresolved. H111 is not supported because the exposed cell has only 25 observations, the point estimate is opposite to the hypothesized direction, and the interval is wide; it is closed unresolved. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 8 appraise update. Accepted set remains empty. Direction convention: -1 positive signed = exposed stronger dependency; +1 positive signed = exposed weaker dependency. Benchmarks approximate: outcome_006/014 0.0093, outcome_015 0.0250, outcome_016 0.0256, outcome_013 0.0269, outcome_008 0.0282, outcome_011 0.0301, outcome_001 0.0415.\n\nPrimary active candidate: H107, outcome_008 feature_055 level_003 vs level_001 within feature_002=1, direction +1, signed +0.0614 CI +0.0181 to +0.1047. Not accepted because lower bound is below benchmark. Requested independent validation of H107. Supporting active claims: H98 overall level_003 vs level_001 (+0.0315, lower near null), H100 level_003 vs level_002 (+0.0321, lower near null), H108 feature_002=0 complement null (+0.0035). Rejected: H104 level_004 vs level_001 (upper below benchmark), plus prior feature_055 positive-association family claims such as H96/H86 context. H99 closed unresolved because null point and only marginal upper bound. H105/H106 feature_034 stratum audits are positive but imprecise and deferred.\n\nOther new screens: H84 and H85 rejected for absent-vs-present feature_030/064 on outcome_015 because upper bounds are below benchmark. H101 closed unresolved due near-zero imprecise outcome_006 result. H102 deferred unresolved: positive outcome_006 feature_064 point but cross-outcome feature_064 results are inconsistent and interval includes null. H111 closed unresolved due tiny exposed cell (n=25), opposite point, and wide interval. If H107 validation is near null, reject/close the reversed feature_055 family. If validation strongly replicates, consider accepting H107 or proposing an explicit feature_055-by-feature_002 interaction claim. All interpretations remain dataset-specific associations.",
